{"name":"Hen of the Woods","hex":"#eed9c4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hen of the woods","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible polypore mushroom, Grifola frondosa"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hen_of_the_woods"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grifola frondosa","blocks":[{"text":"Grifola frondosa, also known as hen-of-the-woods, sheep's head, ram's head, or maitake  in Japanese, is a polypore mushroom that grows at the base of trees, particularly old growth oaks or maples. It is native to China, Europe, and North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Grifola_frondosa_%2829715305790%29.jpg/330px-Grifola_frondosa_%2829715305790%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grifola_frondosa","wikidata":"Q1165686"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Hen_of_the_Woods_%2822602103527%29.jpg/500px-Hen_of_the_Woods_%2822602103527%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Hen_of_the_Woods_%2822602103527%29.jpg/1280px-Hen_of_the_Woods_%2822602103527%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Hen_of_the_Woods_%2822602103527%29.jpg/500px-Hen_of_the_Woods_%2822602103527%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHen_of_the_Woods_(22602103527).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Klapperschwamm.jpg/250px-Klapperschwamm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Klapperschwamm.jpg/500px-Klapperschwamm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb